/*!

@page Snapshot_modes Snapshot Modes


QMMF Server supports Image capture. Capturing image is independent of sessions.
The only pre-condition is Camera to be started. Multiple capture modes are
supported. Image capture could work without additional configuration. Optionally
multiple parameters could be configured, additional post-processing plugins
could be added and one or two thumbnails could be added.

### Image capture APIs ###

1.  __CaptureImage__ - Image capture API. Takes image dimension and format,
number of required snapshots and camera settings. Snapshot stream is created
during first image capture. This leads to camera reconfiguration which produces
gap in ongoing video tracks.

2.  __CancelCaptureImage__ - Aborts ongoing capture and shuts down snapshot
streams. This also leads to camera configuration.

3.  __ConfigImageCapture__ - This API is optional and following settings
could be set:
    +   QMMF_SNAPSHOT_TYPE - QMMF supports multiple snapshot types(modes):

        +   Still capture is the basic snapshot mode. This is the default
        snapshot type. If this mode is selected video tracks are interrupted for
        as many frames as the number of snapshots.

        +  StillPlusRAW capture is same as Still snapshot, but with addition of
        RAW dump.

        +  VideoSnapshot capture is same as Still snapshot, but video tracks are
        not interrupted. Limitation is that video frames which are capture
        together with snapshot have same settings as snapshot.

        +  Continuous mode is streaming capture that generates snapshots until
        CancelCaptureImage API is called. This mode always involves
        post-processing. If the user does not provide any post-processing
        plugins only RAW to YUV and JPEG processing are involved. Frame rate is
        limited to 1 second divided to the slowest post-processing plugin.

        +  ZSL capture mode is enabled whenever this mode is set. At this point
        of time ZSL stream, ZSL queue and reprocess stream are created. Whenever
        capture image happens, one of the frames from ZSL queue is taken and
        reprocessed. ZSL queue could store RAW or YUV frame configuration.

    +   QMMF_POSTPROCESS_PLUGIN - QMMF supports post-process plugins. QMMF
    provides few post-processing plugins, but the client could develop custom
    plugins. This API takes list of plugins. The processing sequence will be
    same as the sequence in the list. First plugin in the list will be executed
    first. This configuration could be combined with all snapshot modes.

    +   QMMF_POSTPROCESS_FRAME_SKIP - This configuration sets frame skip rate
    and could be combined with any snapshot type. Setting of this configuration
    involves post-processing.

    +   QMMF_JPEG_CAPTURE_SETUP - This configuration setups JPEG encoder.
    Setting of this configuration involves post-processing.

    +   QMMF_IMAGE_THUMBNAIL - This configuration could enable and configure
    thumbnail and screennail. Setting of this configuration involves
    post-processing.

    +   QMMF_EXIF - Enables generating of EXIF. Setting of this configuration
    involves post-processing.


### Burst capture ###

Burst capture is sequence of snapshots which are generated of sequential
frames from the sensor. This means that the time between burst frames is
consistent. Burst capture is enabled when number on capture images is higher than
one. Burst capture could be combined with Still, StillPlusRAW and VideoSnapshot.
Continuous capture and ZSL are mutually exclusive with burst capture. Burst
always involves post-processing because usually processing time is longer than
frame rate and multiple buffers are needed to queue pending frames for
post-processing. The maximum supported number of burst capture depends on
available memory and frame rate.



___
*/